Subject: [PATCH 2/2] docs: what a TObject's fBits and fUniqueID are where ROOT
 prints them

The same finding as ae646b4e's message, in the project's docs store: the file holds
fBits & ~0x03000000 and a plain identifier, ROOT's reader puts the heap's two bits and
the ProcessID index + 1 (TBufferIO::GetPidOffset, held in TKey::fSeekPdir's high bits)
on the object, and trying to do it in buffer.py::referenced broke seven round-trip
tests. Nothing here changes behaviour; the io/tree six need the reassembly in
interp.py's element read.
